    <statement><p>The largest set on which the function <m>f(x,y) = \sqrt{x+y} - \sqrt{x-y}</m>
is continuous is <fillin characters="20" name="AnSwEr0001"/></p>
<p><ol label="A.">
<li>
<p>the whole xy-plane</p>
</li>
<li>
<p><m>{ (x,y) | -x \lt  y \lt  x }</m></p>
</li>
<li>
<p><m>{ (x,y) | -x \le y \le x }</m></p>
</li>
<li>
<p><m>{ (x,y) | -x \lt  y \le x }</m></p>
</li>
<li>
<p><m>{ (x,y) | x \ge y }</m></p>
</li>
</ol></p>
</statement>
    <answer>
      <p>C</p>
    </answer>
